<title>UK: IGC trims 1996 coarse grains output estimate.</title>
<headline>IGC trims 1996 coarse grains output estimate.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Grains Council pared its estimate for world 1996 coarse grains production to 881 million tonnes from a previous estimate made in November of 884 million.</p>
<p>Output in 1995 was 790 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The fall from the November figure reflected sharp cuts in data for Russia and Ukraine, the IGC said in its latest market report, issued on Thursday.</p>
<p>The IGC cut its estimate of 1996/97 coarse grains stocks to 110 million tonnes from a previous 114 million and compared with 86 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Latest IGC estimates put Russia's coarse grains output at 31.8 million tonnes, against a previous estimate of 35.5 million</p>
</text>
